<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bappa Rawal</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">8th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bappa Rawal is the legendary founder of the power of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guhila-dynasty">Guhila dynasty</a> in Mewar, said in dynastic tradition to have taken the fort of Chittor from its Mori rulers in the early eighth century. Later inscriptions and bardic accounts made him a devotee of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ekalinga">Ekalinga</a> and a hero of resistance to Arab raids, but his historical identity is uncertain, and scholars still debate which ruler named in inscriptions he may have been.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bappa-rawal.jpg" alt="Bappa Rawal" width="320" height="391" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Historicboyz · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bappa_Rawal.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
